  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Shisheh is a village in the Ahar county of the East Azerbaijan Province of Iran, situated about 40 km northeast of the city Ahar. Near the village a rock inscription of the Urartean king Argi\u0161ti II, son of Rusa, has been found (A 11-6). The inscription reports a military campaign of Argi\u0161ti to the land Arhu (which is apparently the name the Urartians used for the respective region). Furthermore, Argi\u0161ti states that he built a fortress named \u201cstronghold of the god Haldi\u201d (Haldiei irdu\u0161i) and a city at this place.",
